                "text": "Let me understand the rule and create 3 demonstration pairs.\n\nThe verifier: for each column c, if bottom row grid[n-1][c]==7 skip (background). Otherwise treat as bar. Colors rotated right, heights rotated left.\n\nNote: the verifier checks all columns, not just odd. But background 7 columns skipped. Even columns are all 7 so skipped.\n\nI need to author inputs the verifier can evaluate. Let me create 3 varied examples.\n\nLet me think about grid dimensions. The example is 7x7 square. The rule says grid rectangular. Verifier uses n = len(grid) for number of rows, and iterates columns range(n) - assumes square! So inputs must be square, else index error. Let's keep square to be safe.\n\nActually n = len(grid) = rows. range(n) for columns. If square it's fine. Use square grids.\n\nLet me design input grids with orange background 7, bars on odd columns 1,3,5 (for 7-width). Different colors, heights.\n\nExample A: 7x7.\nColumns: 1,3,5.\n- col1: color 9, height 3\n- col3: color 8, height 5\n- col5: color 3, height 2\n\nBottom row: [7,9,7,8,7,3,7]\ncol1 rows 4..6 = 9, col3 rows 2..6 = 8, col5 rows 5..6 = 3.\n\nGrid rows 0-6:\nrow0: 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nrow1: 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nrow2: 7 7 7 8 7 7 7\nrow3: 7 7 7 8 7 7 7\nrow4: 7 9 7 8 7 7 7\nrow5: 7 9 7 8 7 3 7\nrow6: 7 9 7 8 7 3 7\n\nColors [9,8,3] rotate right -> [3,9,8]. Heights [3,5,2] rotate left -> [5,2,3].\n\nOutput bars: col1 color 3 height 5; col3 color 9 height 2; col5 color 8 height 3.\n\nrows:\nrow0: all 7\nrow1: col1=3 (rows1-6 since height5 -> rows 2..6? height5 means rows n-5=2 to 6. So row1 all 7)\nrow2: col1=3, col3=9 (height2 rows5-6)\nrow3: col1=3\nrow4: col1=3\nrow5: col1=3, col3=9, col5=8\nrow6: col1=3, col3=9, col5=8\n\nOutput:\nrow0: 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nrow1: 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nrow2: 7 3 7 7 7 7 7\nrow3: 7 3 7 7 7 7 7\nrow4: 7 3 7 7 7 7 7\nrow5: 7 3 7 9 7 8 7\nrow6: 7 3 7 9 7 8 7\n\nGood.\n\nExample B: different dims, say 9x9. bars on cols 1,3,5,7.\n- col1 color 2 height 4\n- col3 color 5 height 1\n- col5 color 6 height 6\n- col7 color 4 height 3\n\nCheck bottom row: [7,2,7,5,7,6,7,4,7].\n\nGrid 9 rows:\ncol1: rows 5..8 = 2\ncol3: rows 8..8 = 5\ncol5: rows 3..8 = 6\ncol7: rows 6..8 = 4\n\nrows:\nr0: 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7 7\nr1: all 7\nr2: all 7\nr3: col5=6 -> 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7\nr4: 7 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7\nr5: 7 2 7 7 7 6 7 7 7\nr6: 7 2 7 7 7 6 7 4 7\nr7: 7 2 7 7 7 6 7 4 7\nr8: 7 2 7 5 7 6 7 4 7\n\nColors [2,5,6,4] rotate right -> [4,2,5,6]\nHeights [4,1,6,3] rotate left -> [1,6,3,4]\n\nNew bars: col1 color4 height1; col3 color2 height6; col5 color5 height3; col7 color6 height4.\n\nrows (n=9):\ncol1 h1: row8\ncol3 h6: rows3..8\ncol5 h3: rows6..8\ncol7 h4: rows5..8\n\nr0: all7\nr1: all7\nr2: all7\nr3: col3=2: 7 7 7 2 7 7 7 7 7\nr4: 7 7 7 2 7 7 7 7 7\nr5: col3=2, col7=6: 7 7 7 2 7 7 7 6 7\nr6: col3=2, col5=5, col7=6: 7 7 7 2 7 5 7 6 7\nr7: 7 7 7 2 7 5 7 6 7\nr8: col1=4,col3=2,col5=5,col7=6: 7 4 7 2 7 5 7 6 7\n\nExample C: smaller, 5x5, bars cols1,3.\n- col1 color 1 height 2\n- col3 color 6 height 4\n\nBottom row [7,1,7,6,7].\nrows n=5:\ncol1 rows3-4, col3 rows1-4.\nr0: all7\nr1: 7 7 7 6 7\nr2: 7 7 7 6 7\nr3: 7 1 7 6 7\nr4: 7 1 7 6 7\n\nColors [1,6] -> [6,1]; heights [2,4] -> [4,2].\nNew: col1 color6 h4 (rows1-4); col3 color1 h2 (rows3-4).\nr0: all7\nr1: 7 6 7 7 7\nr2: 7 6 7 7 7\nr3: 7 6 7 1 7\nr4: 7 6 7 1 7\n\nThese look good. Let me use the tool to generate outputs (environment computes). I'll call all three.\n\nActually I should call show_transformed_input for each. Let me do that.",
